2548_front.jpg","https://assets.lcsc.com/images/lcsc/900x900/20221229_YAGEO-RC0603FR-071KL_C22548_back.jpg","https://assets.lcsc.com/images/lcsc/900x900/20221229_YAGEO-RC0603FR-071KL_C22548_blank.jpg"],"edaSvgInfo":{"schSvg":"//image.easyeda.com/component_svgs/prod/8e06176593c83cb1ac26267a81465057.svg?t=1732211474","pcbSvg":"//image.easyeda.com/component_svgs/prod/398691f1f785460098bbe5ee6590333c.svg?t=1732211474"},"faqs":[{"question":"How Much Power Can the AMS1117-3.3 Handle in an SOT-223 Package Without Overheating?","answer":"Power dissipation  is calculated as . For the SOT-223 package, the thermal resistance () is approximately . If you drop 5V to 3.3V at 500mA, the  is 0.85W, raising the junction temperature by . To reach the full 1A output, you must provide adequate PCB copper pours as a heat sink. If the differential voltage is high (e.g., 12V to 3.3V), the current must be significantly derated to prevent thermal shutdown."},{"question":"What Is the Minimum Input Voltage Required for the AMS1117-3.3 (C22548) to Provide a Stable 3.3V Output?","answer":"The AMS1117-3.3 is a Low Dropout (LDO) regulator with a typical dropout voltage of 1.1V to 1.3V at 1A load. To ensure a regulated 3.3V output, the input voltage () must be at least 4.5V to 4.6V (). While it can technically handle up to 15V input, using a 5V supply is ideal for minimizing heat dissipation while maintaining regulation."},{"question":"What Are the Recommended Capacitors for the AMS1117-3.3 to Prevent Circuit Oscillation?","answer":"Stability in the AMS1117-3.3 requires an output capacitor with a specific Equivalent Series Resistance (ESR). It is highly recommended to use at least a 22µF Tantalum or Electrolytic capacitor on the output. While Ceramic capacitors are popular, their ultra-low ESR can sometimes cause LDO oscillation; if using ceramics, adding a small series resistor (0.5Ω) or ensuring a minimum of 10µF is crucial for frequency compensation and transient response."},{"question":"Can the AMS1117-3.3 Be Used as a Direct Replacement for LM1117, LD1117, or AZ1117?","answer":"Yes, the AMS1117-3.3 is a functional and pin-to-pin compatible replacement for most industry-standard 1117 series LDOs in the SOT-223 package, including the TI LM1117-3.3 and STMicroelectronics LD1117S33. The pinout is standard: Pin 1 (Adj/GND), Pin 2 (Vout/Tab), Pin 3 (Vin). Always check the maximum input voltage rating, as some variants support up to 15V while others may differ slightly in transient performance."},{"question":"Is the AMS1117-3.3 Suitable for Powering ESP32, ESP8266, or STM32 Microcontrollers?","answer":"Absolutely. The AMS1117-3.3 is a staple in the maker community for powering ESP32 and STM32 modules because these MCUs require a steady 3.3V supply and can have current spikes up to 400mA-600mA during Wi-Fi/Bluetooth transmission. The 1A rating of the C22548 provides ample headroom. For battery-powered IoT devices, however, consider the 5mA quiescent current, which might be higher than specialized ultra-low-power LDOs."}],"pdfUrl":"https://datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/b426be3ce22c6de3e0c3a2248e49159e.pdf?productCode=C22548","authenticationList":["ROHS3 认证"],"isRohsCert":true,"rohsCertType":"ROHS3","rohsCertList":[{"fileCode":"wj1598927","fileName":"YAGEO(国巨)_贴片电容_X6S系列_ROHS认证.pdf","url":"https://datasheet.lcsc.com/certification/rohs/7231f3cca6980a4791d39cd2bf4e90cb.pdf"},{"fileCode":"wj1831512","fileName":"全量通用_ROHS认证_YAGEO(国巨).pdf","url":"https://datasheet.lcsc.com/certification/rohs/880d4dd55fe33a5c283e5964fb88da1d.pdf"},{"fileCode":"wj1851664","fileName":"全量通用_ROHS认证_YAGEO(国巨)@@Brightking(君耀电子).pdf","url":"https://datasheet.lcsc.com/certification/rohs/b66f8cddf95c82a86c072e3fb0621167.pdf"}],"productDescEn":null,"productIntroEn":"100mW 1kΩ 75V Thick Film Resistor ±100ppm/℃ ±1% 0603 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount RoHS","paramVOList":[{"paramCode":"param_10837_n","paramName":"功率","paramNameEn":"Power(Watts)","paramValue":"100mW","paramValueEn":"100mW","paramV